  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Centre<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units</p><p>Equation of tangent at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>On rolling the given circle upward&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;units&nbsp;on&nbsp;the tangent&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>, centre of the circle also moving&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;unit upward, so</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/da7125cf-001c-4292-b4e7-6b03575f1bc6-9896227.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 446px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Centre of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Centre of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp; area of trapezium</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;sq. units</p>",
